<main>
  <section class="community-hero">
    <div class="community-wrap">
      <div class="community-hero-content">
        <h1>We are Sepheo.</h1>
        <p>
          Sepheo is a co-operative for freelance professionals - sharing skills, building teams, and matching people to work. We are self-funded and democratically organised on co-operative principles. Our vision is to support collaboration with, and creation of, aligned organisations.
        </p>
        <div class="community-actions">
          <a href="https://forum.sepheo.co" class="community-button community-button-outline">Visit the forum</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="community-section" id="story">
    <div class="community-wrap">
      <header class="community-section-head">
        <p class="community-label tone-green">About</p>
      </header>

      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="about-narrative">
          <p>
            Sepheo grew out of
            <strong>Code-Operative</strong>, a software co-op founded in 2017                      
            in the North East of England. Over its lifetime Code-Op gave many people
            their first steps into both the co-operative movement and a technology career,
            granting its members a greater degree of autonomy over their economic lives.
          </p>
          <p>
            After years of exploration, the members realised they had to choose between three                      
            incompatible models: recruitment, consultancy, and product development. They chose to
            focus entirely on
            <strong>connecting freelancers to roles within co-ops and aligned organisations.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>So Code-Operative was dissolved with gratitude, and Sepheo was born.</p>
          <p>
            Sepheo sits within a rich ecosystem. We are members of
            <strong>
              <a href="https://www.co-ops.tech">CoTech,</a>
            </strong>
            a network of 40+ UK tech co-operatives,                      
            and were inspired by
            <strong>
              <a href="https://www.happy-dev.fr">Happy Dev,</a>
            </strong>
            a federation                      
            of 300+ freelancers across France. We believe the co-op economy grows faster when its
            organisations support each other. There are a lot of amazing people out there and we want 
            to help you meet them.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="about-aside" aria-label="Sepheo model summary">
          <article class="about-card">
            <p class="about-card-label tone-rose">The name</p>
            <h2>S.E.P.H.E.O.</h2>
            <p>Self-Employed People Helping Each Other. A mutual network run on co-operative principles.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="about-card">
            <p class="about-card-label tone-teal">For Freelancers</p>
            <h2>A support network</h2>
            <p>We do not supply your labour to clients - we support you, and introduce you to client organisations and other freelancers. You need to have the core skills - we can't train you to do your job. But we do plan to partner with people who provide training in a range of areas.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="about-card">
            <p class="about-card-label tone-amber">For Organisations</p>
            <h2>A talent network</h2>
            <p>We do not deliver solutions or services to you - we introduce you to people who can. After the initial introduction, for which we accept a fee to cover our costs, freelancers have a direct relationship with their clients.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

